Done. Round gen_r6 is complete for gen_pfa_large. Summary of what happened:

**Coverage (the surprise-round play).** The entry grew from 4 to 20 supported sizes: every two-stage coprime composite in 14..127 with modules {2,3,4,5,7,8,9,11,13,16,25} and L ≥ 44 — 44, 48, 52, 55, 56, 63, 65, 72, 75, 77, 88, 91, 99, 104, 112, 117 — each a lean GT-PFA instantiation (new generic odd-N module macro for DFT 3/7/9/11/13, reusable DFT8 macro, odd-L phase-2 stash tail, table-driven tune/create). All 16 maps were validated against numpy before writing the C; all pass on the node at 3.5–5.0e-16 rel L2, bit-repeatable, cold create 0.2–3.5 s. 15 of 16 beat MKL at B=1 (1.15x–1.52x); only L=112 (2⁴·7) trails at 0.91x — recorded as next round's target.

**Two bugs caught and fixed along the way.** (1) At odd L the map's `/8` vector count truncated the last 1–3 complex elements per volume — the create() chain gate caught it (wisdom verdict `l75-ip1.x`); fixed with a masked map tail, all 13 lean chain verdicts now store `.ch`, and full chained runs pass at 75 (m=8: 2.38e-14) and 117 (m=6: 5.94e-15). (2) Doubling the translation unit flipped GCC's inlining of map_vec into the scored chain functions — measured +0.9% at L=100 (4/4 held-lease pairs); fixed with per-size noinline constant-count map wrappers, after which the scored winner functions are instruction-identical to the r5 object and A/Bs show no regression (100: 4726 vs 4741+; 50: tie; 40: wash over 5 pairs).

The strategy record has the full Round gen_r6 section, and my wisdom keys are stripped under flock per protocol.

**Technique ended on:** lean GT-PFA class coverage (16 new coprime-composite sizes via one generic odd-N module) on the unchanged r5 two-sweep engine; best wallaby graded-chain: **163.8 us/xform batched (L=40 B=8 m=128)** and **4726 us/xform at B=1 (L=100 m=64)**; rel L2 vs numpy **≤ 5.0e-16** across all 20 supported sizes.
